# Checkout is LF on every platform, whatever the contributor's core.autocrlf says.
# Everything the framework writes into this hub — commands, agents, specs, catalog,
# manifests — is written with LF, and every baseline/spec hash normalizes line
# endings, so a CRLF working tree makes hashes and generated files churn for a reason
# that has nothing to do with the change under test. Without this, the very first
# commit in a freshly created hub rewrites the line endings of every file it just
# received, and warns about it once per file.
# A tree that is already CRLF converges with `git add --renormalize .`.
* text=auto eol=lf
